cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DietView, please cite it as below."
title: "DietView: An R Package for Interactive, Taxonomically Complete Diet Visualization from Stomach-Content Data"
version: 0.1.0
abstract: >-
  DietView turns a long table of stomach-content records into interactive,
  taxonomically complete sunburst views of predator diet. It resolves prey to
  the WoRMS classification, computes per-taxon relative importance in occurrence
  and weight within each taxonomic rank (with unidentified prey kept as an
  explicit NA category), quantifies the identification bias associated with
  digestion level, and renders the whole diet across any user-declared
  covariates as a Shiny app, a self-contained HTML dashboard, or plain plotly
  figures.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Sosthene A. V."
    family-names: "Akia"
    email: "akiasosthene@gmail.com"
  - name: "CADI Gulf Center"
repository-code: "https://github.com/SostheneA/DietView"
url: "https://sosthenea.github.io/DietView/"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - diet analysis
  - stomach contents
  - trophic ecology
  - fisheries
  - WoRMS
  - taxonomy
  - data visualization
  - sunburst
  - R
